  m_text: "The axial skeleton (the green portion of Figure 8.1 on p. 108) can be\xAD
    divided into three parts: the skull, the vertebral column, and the thoracic cage.
    This division of the skeleton forms the longitudinal axis of the body and protects
    the brain, spinal cord, heart, and lungs."
