--- !u!114 &9078383833035125252
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 9078383833035125254}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The ethmoid bone is a delicate, spongy bone located between the eyes at
    the roof of the nasal cavity. It''s a key part of the cranial floor and nasal
    cavity, separating the nasal cavity from the brain. The ethmoid bone consists
    of three main parts: the horizontal cribriform plate, which allows for the passage
    of olfactory nerves; the vertical perpendicular plate, forming part of the nasal
    septum; and the two lateral masses or labyrinths, containing air cells. The ethmoid
    bone also contributes to the eye sockets and contains the superior and middle
    nasal conchae. Injuries or abnormalities to the ethmoid bone can affect the sense
    of smell and lead to sinus-related issues.'
