  m_text: The right zygomatic bone, often called the cheekbone, is a prominent structure
    in the face. It articulates with the frontal, maxillary, sphenoid, and temporal
    bones. The bone provides the lateral contour of the cheek and orbital margin,
    protecting the eye. Injuries to this bone can impact facial aesthetics and may
    require surgical intervention.
