      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Description: The endocardium is the innermost layer of the heart''s walls.
    It lines the heart chambers and covers the heart valves.


    Composition: The
    endocardium is composed of a layer of endothelial cells and an underlying layer
    of connective tissue.


    Function: Its smooth surface allows for the easy
    flow of blood within the heart chambers, preventing blood clots. Additionally,
    it plays a vital role in the contraction of the myocardium (heart muscle) and
    the electrical conduction system of the heart.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
