  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: The sphenoid bone is a complex, butterfly-shaped bone situated in the central
    base of the skull. It articulates with all other cranial bones, making it a key
    structural component of the skull. Comprising a central body and three pairs
    of processes (the greater and lesser wings and the pterygoid processes), it provides
    attachment points for various muscles and houses the sphenoid sinus. The sphenoid
    bone also contains the sella turcica, a saddle-shaped depression that holds the
    pituitary gland. Injuries or abnormalities of the sphenoid bone can impact surrounding
    neural and vascular structures, leading to potential complications.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
