  m_text: 'The heart''s valves regulate one-way blood flow:



    Tricuspid valve:
    Between the right atrium and ventricle, it ensures blood flows only toward the
    right ventricle.


    Pulmonary valve: Between the right ventricle and pulmonary
    artery, it directs blood to the lungs.'
