  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The left nasal bone is one of the two small oblong bones that together
    form the bridge of the nose. It is situated in the midline of the face and articulates
    with its counterpart, the right nasal bone, at the nasal dorsum. Superiorly,
    it connects with the frontal bone, while laterally, it articulates with the frontal
    process of the maxilla. The inferior border of the nasal bone is thicker and
    slightly grooved, allowing for the attachment of the cartilaginous tissues that
    form the flexible part of the nose. The bone serves both a protective function,
    by shielding the nasal passages, and an aesthetic function, by providing shape
    and structure to the nose.

'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
