      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Description: The pulmonary trunk is a major vessel emerging from the right
    ventricle. It soon divides into the left and right pulmonary arteries.



    Location:
    Originates from the superior part of the right ventricle at the front of the
    heart.



    Function: Its main role is to transport oxygen-depleted blood from
    the right ventricle to the lungs. Here, blood releases carbon dioxide and absorbs
    oxygen, then returns to the heart via the pulmonary veins.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
