      m_Calls: []
  m_text: The clavicular notch is a concave, U-shaped indentation located on the
    superior lateral corners of the manubrium of the sternum. Each clavicular notch
    articulates with the sternal end of its respective clavicle, forming the sternoclavicular
    joint. This joint is the sole point of bony attachment between the upper limb
    and the axial skeleton, granting the clavicle its pivotal role as a strut. The
    clavicular notch, along with the associated joint, plays a critical role in permitting
    the wide range of motion of the shoulder girdle while maintaining skeletal continuity
    and stability.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
