  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The skull is the body''s protective framework for the brain and facial
    structures. Comprising 22 bones, it''s split into two groups: the cranial bones,
    which encase the brain, and the facial bones, which shape the face. Key cranial
    bones include the frontal, parietal, and occipital. Main facial bones include
    the maxillae (upper jaw) and mandible (lower jaw). The skull also has openings
    for nerves and blood vessels, ensuring brain communication with the rest of the
    body. Its design balances protection, sensory function, and articulation for
    activities like speech and eating.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
