      m_Calls: []
  m_text: The mandible, commonly known as the lower jawbone, is the largest and strongest
    bone in the face. It supports the lower teeth and provides structure for the
    chin and lower facial contour. The mandible plays a pivotal role in mastication
    (chewing) and speech. Its two main parts are the body (horizontal portion) and
    the rami (two vertical extensions). The mandible articulates with the skull at
    the temporomandibular joints, enabling mouth opening, closing, and side-to-side
    movement. Issues with the mandible can affect jaw alignment, speech, and chewing.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
