      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The let palatine bone is one of a pair of bones located at the back part
    of the nasal cavity and the roof of the mouth. It consists of two main parts:
    the horizontal plate, which forms the posterior section of the hard palate, and
    the perpendicular plate, which contributes to the lateral wall of the nasal cavity.
    It articulates with multiple bones, including the maxilla and sphenoid. The palatine
    bone plays a pivotal role in separating the oral and nasal cavities. Any defects
    or injuries in this area can lead to communication between the two cavities,
    potentially affecting speech, swallowing, and other functions.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
