      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Description: The tricuspid valve, also known as the right atrioventricular
    valve, consists of three leaflets or cusps. This valve facilitates unidirectional
    blood flow, allowing blood to move from the right atrium to the right ventricle
    while preventing backflow.


    Location: Positioned between the right atrium
    and the right ventricle in the heart.


    Function: Its primary function is
    to ensure that blood flows in a single direction: from the right atrium into
    the right ventricle during the relaxation phase (diastole) of the cardiac cycle. '
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
