      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Description: The right auricle, often called the atrial appendage, is
    a small, ear-shaped muscular pouch extending from the right atrium. It has a
    wrinkled appearance, resembling a dog''s ear.


    Location: It projects anteriorly
    from the superior aspect of the right atrium near the superior vena cava''s entrance.


    Function:
    The right auricle plays a minor role in the heart''s overall function. It increases
    the atrium''s volume slightly, allowing for a little more blood to be held. During
    atrial contraction, it ensures that blood is efficiently directed from the atrium
    into the ventricle.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
