  m_text: 'Description: The myocardium is the thickest layer of the heart wall, sandwiched
    between the endocardium (innermost) and the epicardium (outermost).



    Composition:
    Consists largely of cardiac muscle tissue which contracts to pump blood.



    Function:
    It''s responsible for the heart''s contractile force, enabling it to pump blood
    throughout the body. The strength and regularity of heart contractions are determined
    by the myocardium.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
