      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Description: The left pulmonary artery is one of the two branches of the
    pulmonary trunk, conveying deoxygenated blood from the heart to the left lung
    for oxygenation.



    Location: It emerges from the pulmonary trunk, passing
    over the left main bronchus, and directs towards the left lung.



    Function:
    Its main function is to carry deoxygenated blood from the heart to the left lung,
    where it gets oxygenated before returning to the heart.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
